The portable C in the scenario ended: what it is expected to show otherwise
than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/ended.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 1, 7, 8, 14 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the second copy has the memory to run a command, and the program that it
runs stays, also when DOS has ended the copy, which keeps no list of such
programs to release: no screen shows that, since the program that started the
copy clears the screen. The registers that a copy leaves are those of a
program that keeps no list of such programs and has taken neither INT 27h nor
INT 21h, so DX is what the original's is where its setup has TSR manager off,
and DS, which is left out, as it came; and the map of the memory is not looked
at. And the Advanced options have no Quick execute commands: Clear keyboard
buffer and what is below it in the box stand a row further up, the cursor with
them where it is on that box, the box is a row shorter, and the two rows that
its last row and the shadow below it were on show what is behind the box, the
upper one in the shadow

